  "description": "BigP3BCI Study B is a multi-session EEG dataset from 19 ALS patients performing a P300-based brain-computer interface speller task using a 6x6 checkerboard visual stimulus paradigm. The dataset comprises 8 sessions per subject with 16-channel EEG recordings sampled at 256 Hz, annotated with HED 8.4.0 tags for target and non-target visual events. This derivative dataset is part of the larger BigP3BCI collection.",
  "methods_description": "EEG data were acquired using a g.USBamp amplifier (g.tec) with 16 channels in standard 10-20 montage at 256 Hz sampling rate. The experimental paradigm employed a 6x6 checkerboard visual stimulus presentation with target and non-target event classification.",
